---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Changelog - Makonome">
  <main>
    <header>
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to home</a>
      <h1>Changelog</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">All notable changes to Makonome</p>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog">
      <article class="version">
        <h2>1.0.4 <span class="date">October 2026</span></h2>
        <p class="version-note">The Accuracy Trainer is part of Makonome Pro. Turn it on in Settings → Experimental. The Mac version is coming soon to the Mac App Store.</p>
        <div class="changes">
          <h3>Added</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Accuracy Trainer: connect an electronic drum kit over MIDI and see live timing for every hit, with a per-drum breakdown, histograms and a beat map</li>
            <li>Tightness slider to set how strict the timing bands are</li>
            <li>Free Time mode: after a count-in the click goes silent and Makonome follows your tempo, showing your drift bar by bar</li>
            <li>Practice mode hides the numbers while you play and reveals a short summary every 4 or 8 bars</li>
            <li>Record trainer sessions, browse them later, and share them</li>
            <li>Makonome now runs natively on Mac, with keyboard shortcuts (Space to play or stop, arrows for tempo), a menu bar menu, and the trainer in its own window</li>
            <li>Choose the scoring grid (quarter, eighth, sixteenth, triplet) and focus on a single drum</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Hits are now scored against when you actually hear the click, not when it was scheduled</li>
            <li>The trainer reconnects to your MIDI device after the Mac wakes from sleep</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="version">
        <h2>1.0.3 <span class="date">March 2026</span></h2>
        <div class="changes">
          <h3>Added</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Ableton Link: sync tempo, start/stop and beat phase with other Link apps and devices on your network</li>
            <li>Link indicator in the toolbar with a status sheet</li>
            <li>Latency offset slider for fine-tuning Link sync per device</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Link beats no longer arrive late compared to other devices</li>
            <li>Link stays in sync at high tempos (above 300 BPM)</li>
            <li>Voice count accents no longer sound pitch-shifted</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="version">
        <h2>1.0.2 <span class="date">March 2026</span></h2>
        <div class="changes">
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Paywall showed a spinner on both buttons at once</li>
            <li>"Woodblock" label was cut off on smaller screens</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="version">
        <h2>1.0.1 <span class="date">March 2026</span></h2>
        <div class="changes">
          <h3>Added</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Pause and resume for practice sessions</li>
            <li>Four full-screen beat visualizations: Pendulum, Circular, Count and Line, with a swipeable carousel</li>
            <li>Voice count sound: spoken beat numbers</li>
            <li>Better tempo detection with two switchable engines</li>
            <li>Optional 0.5 BPM steps (experimental)</li>
            <li>Home Screen Quick Actions: Start Metronome and Start Practice</li>
            <li>Collections: group presets into practice routines or setlists</li>
            <li>Preset favorites, duplication and notes</li>
            <li>Practice Stats widget (small and medium)</li>
            <li>iCloud backup option</li>
            <li>Time-based tempo changer mode with live countdown display</li>
            <li>Gap Trainer progressive mode: gaps automatically grow longer each cycle</li>
            <li>Sound preview when switching sounds</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Changed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You can still browse, load and delete saved presets and collections after the trial ends</li>
            <li>Trial start date now survives app reinstall</li>
            <li>"Premium" is now called "Pro"</li>
            <li>Sound picker and pitch slider moved into the volume sheet</li>
            <li>Updated look for iOS 26</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Tab switching from deep links when the app was already running</li>
            <li>Tempo changer time mode not triggering correctly</li>
            <li>Crash when tapping beat indicators during time-based tempo changes</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="version">
        <h2>1.0.0-beta <span class="date">June 2025</span></h2>
        <p class="version-note">Initial beta release.</p>
        <div class="changes">
          <h3>Added</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Core metronome with sample-accurate timing (AVAudioEngine)</li>
            <li>Adjustable BPM (40-400) with tap tempo</li>
            <li>Time signatures from 1 to 16 beats per bar</li>
            <li>Subdivisions: quarter, eighth, sixteenth, triplets</li>
            <li>Per-beat accent and mute controls</li>
            <li>Multiple click sounds: click, clave, woodblock, cowbell</li>
            <li>Pitch adjustment for click sounds</li>
            <li>Gap Trainer for internalized timing practice</li>
            <li>Tempo Changer for gradual speed increases</li>
            <li>Practice session tracking with history</li>
            <li>Preset save/load system</li>
            <li>Haptic feedback (experimental)</li>
            <li>Tempo detection via microphone (experimental)</li>
            <li>Dark theme support</li>
            <li>Background audio playback</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <p>&copy; 2025 Makonome. Built with ♥ for musicians.</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  header {
    padding: 2rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .changelog {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .version {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .version.unreleased {
    border-color: var(--color-accent-dim);
    border-style: dashed;
  }

  .version h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .date {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: normal;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .version-note {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .changes h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .changes h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .changes ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .changes li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .changes li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid #333;
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding: 2rem 0;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
